From d87c175b83250f2fc2afd02cb64aff7b01eccc01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:52:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: restore IRIS1 CPU clock configuration on enable

The VPU5 downstream clock enable hook clears CPU_CGC_DIS and
CPU_CLOCK_CONFIG after the clocks are prepared. Do the same after a
successful core clock enable on IRIS1, including runtime resume. The
no-TZ reset helper is not used by the normal authenticated firmware path.

Reference: Android Q venus_hfi.c clock_config_on_enable_vpu5() and its
call in __prepare_enable_clks(), downstream 192eca8550f95c.

Only two IRIS1-specific MMIO writes are added. Clock rates, power-domain
selection and reset sequencing are deliberately separate changes.
Hardware validation: cold boot and repeated idle/resume of both codec
sessions; host compilation cannot validate the power sequence.

Signed-off-by: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
index f0269524a..5d04a57c5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
@@ -70,6 +70,11 @@ static int core_clks_enable(struct venus_core *core)
 			goto err;
 	}
 
+	if (IS_IRIS1(core)) {
+		writel(0, core->wrapper_base + WRAPPER_CPU_CGC_DIS);
+		writel(0, core->wrapper_base + WRAPPER_CPU_CLOCK_CONFIG);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 err:
 	while (i--)
-- 
2.43.0

